# Design and image files: never normalise line endings, never try to diff them.
# Git's own binary detection would catch most of these, but "probably" is not a
# good property for the only copy of a part that has been fitted and works.
#
# STEP is the odd one: ISO 10303-21 is a text format, so git could diff it. It is
# marked binary anyway. A diff of a few thousand renumbered CARTESIAN_POINT lines
# tells you nothing, and freezing the bytes keeps the file identical to what the
# CAD tool exported.
*.3mf     binary
*.3MF     binary
*.sldprt  binary
*.SLDPRT  binary
*.step    binary
*.STEP    binary
*.stl     binary
*.STL     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
